            "learn": {
                "paragraphs": [
                    "**1. X-intercepts:** The zeroes of a polynomial $p(x)$ are the x-coordinates of the points where the graph of $y = p(x)$ intersects the **x-axis**.",
                    "**2. Degree vs Zeroes:** A polynomial of degree $n$ can have **at most $n$ zeroes**.",
                    "**3. Linear:** Degree 1 \\Rightarrow straight line, 1 zero.",
                    "**4. Quadratic:** Degree 2 \\Rightarrow parabola, at most 2 zeroes."
